ts the fields inside <code>recent_meetings</code> (result, goals, competition, date).</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 4. The built block: dates without the year (&ldquo;25 Jan&rdquo; is 2025, the next row&rsquo;s &ldquo;31 Aug&rdquo; is 2024), competition codes (BL1), totals and a bar that read as all-time, and &ldquo;First-ever meeting&rdquo; for a pair the data has not seen meet.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><section aria-label="Head to head"> <div class="sechead"> <span class="eyebrow">Head to head</span>  </div> <div class="h2h-last">First-ever meeting</div> </section></div><section class="mk-p mk-chg" aria-label="Head to head"><div class="sechead"><span class="eyebrow">Head to head</span><span class="mk-n">5</span></div><p class="tt-intro">No meetings on record.</p><div class="mk-h2h"></div></section> <div class="mk-src"><b>Data</b><table><tr><th>On the page</th><th>Comes from</th><th>When it is missing</th></tr><tr><td>Borussia Dortmund &middot; SV Werder Bremen</td><td>the header's names (block 2)</td><td>a name: left out</td></tr><tr><td>Table &middot; Top scorers</td><td>site text, <code>table</code>, <code>topScorers</code></td><td>never missing</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. None of the four chips is a link, although every target is built: the team pages, the league table on the competition's Overview tab, the top scorers on its Rankings tab. The chip is no element of the block standard; the team page shows the same two inert chips (Table, Top scorers) under its fixtures.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><section aria-label="Explore"> <div class="sechead"> <span class="eyebrow">Explore</span>  </div> <div class="linkrow"> <span class="linkchip">Borussia Dortmund</span><span class="linkchip">SV Elversberg</span><span class="linkchip">Table</span><span class="linkchip">Top scorers</span> </div> </section></div><div class="mk-p mk-gone"><span class="mk-n">6</span> The Explore block leaves: its links are the team names above and the breadcrumb.</div> <d