 is W and a match settled on penalties is D</td><td>fewer than five: fewer pills</td></tr><tr><td>incl. DFB-Pokal, UEFA Champions League</td><td><code>mart_team_momentum.contributing_competitions</code>, named by <code>mart_competition_index.competition_name</code></td><td>own competition only: no &ldquo;incl.&rdquo; part</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. None of the 16 value columns has a not-null test; 11 of them have only a not-negative test, no upper bound (the 5 percentages are held to 0&ndash;1, clean sheets to 0&ndash;games).</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 2. The page picks between two marts by phase; the choice is a rule of the matrix, so one mart should serve each side's window for the match, with its <code>window_type</code>, and the page only show it.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 3. The Last 5 caption shows competition codes (&ldquo;DFBP, UCL&rdquo;); the W/D/L letters are English on the German and Finnish pages (the site says S/U/N and V/T/H elsewhere); the Defending sub-label is English in all three.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 4. Every value is rounded in the browser (<code>format.ts</code>); rounding in the browser is the defect #108 names.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 5. Discipline needs each team's yellow and red cards over its window: <code>mart_team_momentum</code> gains them from <code>int_legs__team_match</code>, the source the season totals already use, withheld when a match in the window has no statistics line.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><section aria-label="Form comparison"> <div class="sechead"> <span class="eyebrow">Form comparison</span>  </div><p class="tt-intro mk-p mk-chg">Form metrics from each team&rsquo;s last 5 matches across all competitions. <a class="mk-chevlink" href="/en/glossary/">Metric Glossary<svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></a> <span cl