raws_last5</code>, <code>.losses_last5</code>, the row for (home team, away team); the names: the header's (block 2)</td><td>never missing while the row exists: tested to sum to <code>meetings_last5</code>; each split has its own wording (&ldquo;All of the last 3 meetings were drawn&rdquo;, &ldquo;SV Werder Bremen won the last meeting&rdquo;); no row: &ldquo;No meetings on record&rdquo; in place of the list</td></tr><tr><td>which meetings, newest first</td><td><code>.recent_meetings[]</code>, its first 5</td><td>fewer meetings: fewer rows</td></tr><tr><td>0&ndash;2 SV Werder Bremen &ndash; Borussia Dortmund</td><td>which side was at home: <b>not served</b> (gap 1); the goals: <code>.recent_meetings[].goals_for</code>, <code>.goals_against</code>, in the match's order; the names: the header's (block 2)</td><td>not tested (gap 3)</td></tr><tr><td>Bundesliga &middot; 16 May 2026</td><td><code>.recent_meetings[].league_code</code>, named by <code>mart_competition_index.competition_name</code>; <code>.kickoff_datetime</code>, its UTC day until #146</td><td>not tested (gap 3)</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. Which side was at home in a past meeting is not served: <code>recent_meetings</code> carries no <code>home_away</code>, while <code>int_legs__team_match</code>, the model the mart is built from, has it. One field added to the existing mart; its one reader is the export's match payload. The mock reads it from a stand-in read once from <code>core.fct_fixture</code>.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 2. The mart's descriptions say &ldquo;all time&rdquo; (the table and <code>total_meetings</code>), which is false: it counts only the meetings inside the data window, set per competition in the registry (the Bundesliga's last 10 seasons, the DFB-Pokal's last 5, the European cups' last 10), and BigQuery shows the false text. A competition the site does not hold (the DFL-Supercup) is never counted, here or in the form's last 5.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 3. Nothing tests the fields inside <code>recent_meetings</code> (result, goals, competition, date).</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 4. The built block: dates without the year (&ldquo;25 Jan&rdquo; is 2025, the next row&rsquo;s &ldquo;31 Aug&rdquo; is 2024), competition codes (BL1), totals and a bar that read as all-time, and &ldquo;First-ever meeting&rdquo; for a pair the data has not seen meet.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><section aria-label="Head to head"> <div class="sechead"> <span class="eyebrow">Head to head</span>  </div> <div class="h2h-last">First-ever meeting</div> </section></div><section class="mk-p mk-chg" aria-label="Head to head"><div class="sechead"><span class="eyebrow">Head to head</span><span class="mk-n">5</span></div><p class="tt-intro">No meetings on record.</p><div class="mk-h2h"></div></section><div class="mk-src"><b>Data</b><table><tr><th>On the page</th><th>Comes from</th><th>When it is missing</th></tr><tr><td>which matches</td><td>each of the two teams' next fixture in any competition, from <code>mart_team_fixtures</code> (the team page reads the same mart); a team whose next match is this one adds none. The mock reads the exported fixtures after the export day</td><td>a team with no fixture left: no row</td></tr><tr><td>Bundesliga</td><td>the fixture's <code>league_code</code>, named by <code>mart_competition_index</code></td><td>a name: not guaranteed (block 1, gap 1)</td></tr><tr><td>the two clubs, crests, 18:30, 9 Oct</td><td>the fixture's two teams, the side at home first; its kick-off (UTC until #146)</td><td>no time: &ldquo;TBC&rdquo;, as every match row</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. <code>mart_team_fixtures.upcoming_rank</code> counts per competition (team, competition, season), so rank 1 is the next match in each competition, not the next one overall. The mart gains a rank across all the team's competitions.</div></div><section class="mk-p mk-chg" aria-label="Next matches"><div class="sechead"><span class="eyebrow">Next matches</sp