t</code>, its first 5, newest first</td><td>not tested (gap 3)</td></tr><tr><td>2&ndash;0</td><td><code>.recent_meetings[].goals_for</code>, <code>.goals_against</code>, from the home team's side</td><td>not tested (gap 3)</td></tr><tr><td>SV Werder Bremen</td><td>the away team's name (block 2); which side was at home: <b>not served</b> (gap 1)</td><td>a name: not guaranteed (block 1, gap 1)</td></tr><tr><td>Bundesliga &middot; 16 May 2026</td><td><code>.recent_meetings[].league_code</code>, named by <code>mart_competition_index.competition_name</code>; <code>.kickoff_datetime</code>, its UTC day until #146, with the year</td><td>not tested (gap 3)</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. Which side was at home in a past meeting is not served: <code>recent_meetings</code> carries no <code>home_away</code>, while <code>int_legs__team_match</code>, the model the mart is built from, has it. One field added to the existing mart; its one reader is the export's match payload. The mock's rows carry no H or A for that reason.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 2. The mart's descriptions say &ldquo;all time&rdquo; (the table and <code>total_meetings</code>), which is false: it counts only the meetings inside the data window, set per competition in the registry (the Bundesliga's last 10 seasons, the DFB-Pokal's last 5, the European cups' last 10), and BigQuery shows the false text. A competition the site does not hold (the DFL-Supercup) is never counted, here or in the form's last 5.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 3. Nothing tests the fields inside <code>recent_meetings</code> (result, goals, competition, date).</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 4. The built block: dates without the year (&ldquo;25 Jan&rdquo; is 2025, the next row&rsquo;s &ldquo;31 Aug&rdquo; is 2024), competition codes (BL1), totals and a bar that read as all-time, and &ldquo;First-ever meeting&rdquo; for a pair the data has not seen meet.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><section aria-label="Head to head"> <div class="se