d><td>never missing</td></tr><tr><td>the two names</td><td><code>core.dim_team.team_name</code> (block 2 moves it to <code>mart_competition_fixtures</code>)</td><td>left blank</td></tr><tr><td>Regular Season - 5</td><td><code>core.fct_fixture.round_name</code>, the provider's English</td><td>left out</td></tr><tr><td>met 18 times: 11&ndash;5&ndash;2</td><td><code>mart_head_to_head.total_meetings</code>, <code>.wins</code>, <code>.draws</code>, <code>.losses</code></td><td>never met: the shorter template without it</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. The meetings are only those inside the data's window, which is set per competition: the Bundesliga's 10 seasons (so since 2016/17), most other competitions only the current season. The mart's column description says &ldquo;all time&rdquo;, which is false, and BigQuery shows it.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 2. The page's description for search results reuses <code>aboutNoH2h</code> with the provider's English round name.</div></div><div class="mk-b"><div class="lede"> <p>Borussia Dortmund vs SV Werder Bremen · Regular Season - 5. The two clubs have met 18 times: 11–5–2.</p> </div></div><div class="mk-p mk-gone"><span class="mk-n">8</span> The sentence leaves: every fact it could hold is shown by a block below it (the form comparison, the head to head). The page&rsquo;s one-line summary for search results is its description, which is not shown on the page.</div> <div class="mk-src"><b>Data</b><table><tr><th>On the page</th><th>Comes from</th><th>When it is missing</th></tr><tr><td>the switch, the group names, the 16 labels</td><td>site text, in each language; which rows, their groups and order: the locked <code>metrics_display.md</code> and <code>metric_catalogue</code></td><td>never missing</td></tr><tr><td>which window a team shows</td><td>the phase rules, <code>docs/metrics_context_model.md</code> &sect;3&ndash;4, per team and competition edition: while it runs, <code>mart_team_momentum</code> (<code>window_type</code> last_5, this season only); before the team's first match in a league, <code>mart_team_season_record</code> (<code>window_type</code> prev_season)</td><td>neither served: the block says there are no matches yet</td></tr><tr><td>the 16 values, while a league runs</td><td><code>mart_team_momentum</code>, up to the last 5 finished matches in all the club's competitions this season: <code>goals_per_match</code>, <code>goals_against_per_match</code>, <code>clean_sheets</code>, <code>shots_per_match</code>, <code>shots_inside_box_pct</code>, <code>shots_on_goal_per_match</code>, <code>finishing_efficiency_pct</code>, <code>passes_per_match</code>, <code>passes_accuracy_pct</code>, <code>passes_key_per_match</code>, <code>duels_per_match</code>, <code>duels_won_pct</code>, <code>defensive_actions_per_match</code>, <code>saves_pct</code>, <code>corners_per_match</code>, <code>corners_against_per_match</code></td><td>one side missing: &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; on that side; both missing: the row is left out</td></tr><tr><td>the 16 values, before a team's first match in a league</td><td><code>mart_team_season_record</code>, the same columns, last season in this league (<code>window_type</code> prev_season)</td><td>as above</td></tr><tr><td>the link &ldquo;What the metrics mean&rdquo;</td><td>the glossary page: not built, its address a placeholder, its definitions not written yet (the catalogue's <code>description</code> is technical and English only)</td><td>until the page exists, nothing links</td></tr><tr><td>Discipline: yellow cards, red cards</td><td>nothing serves them for the window: the catalogue's <code>cards_yellow</code>, <code>cards_red</code> are season totals, and <code>mart_team_momentum</code> has no card columns</td><td>shown as &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; until served (gap 5)</td></tr><tr><td>the five W/D/L pills, newest first</td><td><code>mart_team_momentum_window.result</code>, ordered by <code>recency_rank</code>; read from the final score, so a win after extra time is W and a match settled on penalties is D</td><td>fewer than five: fewer pills</td></tr><tr><td>incl. DFB-Pokal, UEFA Champions League</td><td><code>mart_team_momentum.contributing_competitions</code>, named by <code>mart_competition_index.competition_name</code></td><td>own competition only: no &ldquo;incl.&rdquo; part</td></tr></table><div class="mk-gap">Gap 1. None of the 16 value columns has a not-null test; 11 of them have only a not-negative test, no upper bound (the 5 percentages are held to 0&ndash;1, clean sheets to 0&ndash;games).</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 2. The page picks between two marts by phase; the choice is a rule of the matrix, so one mart should serve each side's window for the match, with its <code>window_type</code>, and the page only show it.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 3. The Last 5 caption shows competition codes (&ldquo;DFBP, UCL&rdquo;); the W/D/L letters are English on the German and Finnish pages (the site says S/U/N and V/T/H elsewhere); the Defending sub-label is English in all three.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 4. Every value is rounded in the browser (<code>format.ts</code>); rounding in the browser is the defect #108 names.</div><div class="mk-gap">Gap 5. Discipline needs each team's yellow and red cards over its window: <code>mart_team_momentum</code> gains them from <code>int_legs__team_match</code>, the source the season totals already use, withheld when a match in the window has no statistics line.</div></div><section aria-label="Form comparison"> <div class="sechead"> <span class="eyebrow">Form comparison</span>  </div><p class="tt-intro mk-p mk-chg">Form metrics from each team&rsquo;s last 5 matches across all competitions. <a class="mk-chevlink" href="/en/glossary/">Metric Glossary<svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></a> <span class="mk-n"